{"id":"n-20261016-o34zqk","category":"business","display_title":"Alfred Akirov Delisting Plan","display_title_he":"תוכנית מחיקת המניות של אלפרד אקירוב","short_summary":"At 85, Israeli tycoon Alfred Akirov is seeking to delist Alrov Real Estate from the stock exchange while continuing his long-running pursuit of controlling Clal Insurance.","english_level":"C1","words":465,"reading_time":3,"image":null,"sources":[{"name":"Globes","domain":"globes.co.il","url":"https://www.globes.co.il/news/article.aspx?did=1001559427","title":"אקירוב בגיל 85: \"אני לא יכול לצאת לפנסיה - זה יעשה אותי חולה\"","published_at":"2026-10-16T03:53:00.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-16T03:53:00.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-16T05:51:45.978Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":9,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["At eighty-five years of age, veteran Israeli businessman Alfred Akirov remains deeply active in the commercial world, declaring that retirement is entirely out of the question because inactivity would undoubtedly make him ill. The founder and controlling shareholder of Alrov Real Estate is currently orchestrating a major maneuver to purchase the remaining shares held by the public and delist the company from the Tel Aviv Stock Exchange. Akirov notes that the local stock market severely undervalues the company, as its shares trade significantly below their net asset value and suffer from persistently low market liquidity. His family already holds an impressive eighty-eight percent stake, and the proposed buyout is valued at approximately seven hundred and eighty-eight million shekels, funded entirely through existing cash flow rather than risky new loans.","Market analysts strongly suggest that taking Alrov private serves a dual purpose, potentially clearing crucial regulatory hurdles for Akirov to increase his significant stake in Clal Insurance. For several years, Akirov has sought to secure a controlling interest of thirty percent in Clal Insurance, but the Capital Market Authority has repeatedly rejected his formal requests. By converting Alrov into a private entity, he ultimately hopes to remove specific structural barriers dictated by local centralization laws. This financial endeavor has already proven remarkably lucrative; Alrov's initial investment of six hundred and ninety million shekels in Clal shares has surged in value to over three billion shekels amid a broader market rally in financial sector equities.","Beyond domestic financial battles, Alrov's prestigious luxury hospitality portfolio continues to generate international headlines. Earlier this year, the production team for the popular HBO series The White Lotus rented out every single room and suite at the historic Hotel Lutetia in Paris. The luxury hotel was completely sealed off to regular guests for the exclusive filming of the upcoming television season. According to company disclosures and average room pricing, the high-profile television production paid approximately twenty-eight million shekels for the exclusive takeover, capitalizing on the typically quiet month of August in the French capital. The Lutetia proudly stands alongside other distinguished properties in Alrov's global portfolio, including the David Citadel and Mamilla hotels in Jerusalem, as well as the renowned Hotel Cafe Royal in London and the Conservatorium in Amsterdam.","Akirov's extensive business career spans many decades, beginning after his military service when he joined his father's construction business, followed by brief ventures in textiles and aviation before returning permanently to real estate in the late nineteen-seventies. Despite past controversies, including public clashes with insurance executives and prior disagreements regarding corporate transactions, Akirov maintains that long-term business resilience relies on disciplined cash flow management and unwavering dedication. As he navigates complex regulatory challenges and corporate restructuring, Akirov firmly insists that his personal commitment to the business world remains as steadfast as ever."],"facts":[{"fact":"Alfred Akirov is 85 years old, serves as the founder and controlling shareholder of Alrov Real Estate, and states he has no intention of retiring.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Alrov is planning to buy out public shareholders in Alrov Real Estate for approximately 788 million shekels and delist the company from the Tel Aviv Stock Exchange.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"The production team of HBO's The White Lotus rented the entire Hotel Lutetia in Paris, closing it down and paying roughly 28 million shekels for the stay.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Akirov has faced three rejections from the Capital Market Authority regarding his attempts to gain control of Clal Insurance.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Alrov's investment in Clal Insurance, which cost 690 million shekels, has grown significantly to over 3 billion shekels due to a surge in financial stocks.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Akirov's net worth is estimated at approximately 6.3 billion shekels.","sources":[1]}],"glossary":[{"text":"At","lemma":"at","pos":"ADP","he":"ב־","name":"false"},{"text":"eighty-five","lemma":"eighty-five","pos":"NUM","he":"שמונהים וחמש","name":false},{"text":"years","lemma":"year","pos":"NOUN","he":"שנים","name":false},{"text":"of","lemma":"of","pos":"ADP","he":"של","name":false},{"text":"age","lemma":"age","pos":"NOUN","he":"גיל","name":false},{"text":"veteran","lemma":"veteran","pos":"ADJ","he":"וותיק","name":false},{"text":"Israeli","lemma":"israeli","pos":"ADJ","he":"ישראלי","name":"false"},{"text":"businessman","lemma":"businessman","pos":"NOUN","he":"איש עסקים","name":false},{"text":"Alfred","lemma":"alfred","pos":"PROPN","he":"אלפרד","name":"true"},{"text":"Akirov","lemma":"akirov","pos":"PROPN","he":"אקירוב","name":"true"},{"text":"remains","lemma":"remain","pos":"VERB","he":"נשאר","name":false},{"text":"deeply","lemma":"deeply","pos":"ADV","he":"עמוקות","name":f